// Jest Snapshot v1, https://jestjs.io/docs/snapshot-testing

exports[`broken login screen reports every issue 1`] = `
"expect(element).toBeAccessible()

Found 7 accessibility violations:

1. [image-label-required] Image has no label and is not marked as decorative.
   Element: <Image> in BrokenLoginScreen
   Fix: Add accessibilityLabel (or alt) describing the image. If it is decorative, mark it in a way both platforms understand: alt="", aria-hidden, or accessible={false}.
   Standard: WCAG 1.1.1 Non-text Content (A) · EN 301 549 11.1.1.1
   Docs: https://github.com/lassiecoder/react-native-accessibility-audit/blob/main/docs/rules.md#image-label-required

2. [input-label-required] Text input has only a placeholder ("Email"). Placeholders disappear once someone types, so they aren't a reliable label.
   Element: <TextInput> in BrokenLoginScreen
   Fix: Add accessibilityLabel (or aria-label) describing the field, usually the same text as its visible label. A placeholder is not a label: it disappears once someone types.
   Standard: WCAG 3.3.2 Labels or Instructions (A); 4.1.2 Name, Role, Value (A) · EN 301 549 11.3.3.2, 11.4.1.2
   Docs: https://github.com/lassiecoder/react-native-accessibility-audit/blob/main/docs/rules.md#input-label-required

3. [no-empty-text] Text element has no content.
   Element: <Text> in BrokenLoginScreen
   Fix: Remove the empty Text, or render it only when it has content. Empty text creates a silent stop for screen readers.
   Standard: Best practice (no specific WCAG criterion)
   Docs: https://github.com/lassiecoder/react-native-accessibility-audit/blob/main/docs/rules.md#no-empty-text

4. [interactive-role-required] Interactive element has no role.
   Element: Pressable → <View> in BrokenLoginScreen
   Fix: Add accessibilityRole (or role), e.g. "button" or "link", so screen readers announce what the element does.
   Standard: WCAG 4.1.2 Name, Role, Value (A) · EN 301 549 11.4.1.2
   Docs: https://github.com/lassiecoder/react-native-accessibility-audit/blob/main/docs/rules.md#interactive-role-required

5. [interactive-label-required] Interactive element has no label or text, so screen readers can only announce its role.
   Element: Pressable → <View> in BrokenLoginScreen
   Fix: Add accessibilityLabel (or aria-label), or render visible Text inside the element.
   Standard: WCAG 4.1.2 Name, Role, Value (A) · EN 301 549 11.4.1.2
   Docs: https://github.com/lassiecoder/react-native-accessibility-audit/blob/main/docs/rules.md#interactive-label-required

6. [state-required] Element with role "checkbox" does not expose a checked state.
   Element: Pressable → <View> role="checkbox" name="Remember me" in BrokenLoginScreen
   Fix: Set accessibilityState={{ checked }} (or aria-checked) on checkboxes, radios, switches and toggle buttons; set accessibilityValue (or aria-valuenow / aria-valuetext) on adjustable controls.
   Standard: WCAG 4.1.2 Name, Role, Value (A) · EN 301 549 11.4.1.2
   Docs: https://github.com/lassiecoder/react-native-accessibility-audit/blob/main/docs/rules.md#state-required

7. [no-nested-interactive] Interactive element is nested inside another interactive element.
   Element: Pressable → <View> role="button" name="Continue" in BrokenLoginScreen
   Fix: Move the inner control out of the outer one, or remove accessible={true} from the grouping View. Screen readers focus the outer element as one item, so the inner control cannot be reached.
   Standard: WCAG 2.1.1 Keyboard (A); 4.1.2 Name, Role, Value (A) · EN 301 549 11.2.1.1, 11.4.1.2
   Docs: https://github.com/lassiecoder/react-native-accessibility-audit/blob/main/docs/rules.md#no-nested-interactive"
`;
